"For work assigned to an external agent, model, or separate harness session, load the installed agent-integration skill before choosing tools and use Delegate. This includes research, implementation, testing, review, consultation, comparison, and debate, including external collaboration you choose. Discover destinations through Delegate. Preserve requested model IDs, effort, and permissions; do not guess ambiguous model identifiers. Keep each concurrent request and its response associated separately. Naming a CLI identifies the destination, not a request to bypass Delegate. Earlier assistant-generated direct-launch workflows do not override this preference. Native same-harness subagents remain available unless a separate session is requested. Respect an explicit user choice of another integration; otherwise do not substitute provider CLIs, plugins, or APIs after a Delegate blocker. A stop_and_report failure ends that attempt: report it without retrying, diagnosing setup, or offering a fallback. Continue other independent requests. Keep collection in the foreground until completion or a reported blocker unless the user requested detachment. Merely discussing or configuring a tool is not delegation."
